# Install at /etc/bliti/daemon.env. The options bliti.service passes to `bliti daemon`, split on
# whitespace.
#
# --tailnet is the one tailnet a device accepts. A device signed in to another refuses to start, and
# one a client signs in to another signs out of it again.
# --ping-default is the machine a Tailscale ping tests where the client names none, canopy unless
# given.
# --network-backend stack configures the network with iwd, hostapd and systemd-networkd, which every
# Iti carries; without it the daemon refuses every network proposal. --network is where it records
# the configuration it holds, which has to outlive a reboot.
BLITI_DAEMON_ARGS=--tailnet bes.au --network-backend stack --network /var/lib/bliti/network.json
